body:
i'm on 4.4.1.stable win10 and have the same issue with the new get_length() implementation.


https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/49a5bc7b616bd04689a2c89e89bda41f50241464/drivers/windows/file_access_windows_pipe.cpp#L105-L111
at line 109 fails me in the loop of reading the get_line() outputs after getting the last line and BEFORE the next get_length() test i wrote. also get_error always returns OK even after it throws the error.
it seems to me that instead of throwing an error here it should just return 0 if nothing is available.
upon further testing. i need to use 
```gdscript
var cmdPid :Dictionary
var IO: FileAccess
var IOError: FileAccess

func _process(delta: float) -> void:
	if(IO):
		if(IO.is_open()):
			if(IO.get_length() > 0):
				var buffer:PackedByteArray = IO.get_buffer(IO.get_length())
				var text : String = buffer.get_string_from_utf8()
				cmd_output_label.append_text(text + "\n")
	if(cmdPid):
		if(cmdPid.has("pid")):
			var exitcode = OS.get_process_exit_code(cmdPid["pid"])
			if(exitcode != -1):
				print(exitcode)
				IO = null
				IOError = null
				cmdPid.clear()
```
for it to not throw the error.
